    "overview": "Show what you know about converting units, area, perimeter, time and line plots.",
    "problems": [
      {
        "prompt": "How many inches are in 6 feet?"
      },
      {
        "prompt": "How many grams are in 5 kilograms?"
      },
      {
        "prompt": "How many minutes are in 2 hours and 15 minutes?"
      },
      {
        "prompt": "A rectangle is 14 centimeters long and 8 centimeters wide. Find its area and its perimeter."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "A rectangle has an area of 63 square meters and a width of 7 meters. How long is it?"
      },
      {
        "prompt": "A movie starts at 3:45 p.m. and lasts 1 hour and 50 minutes. What time does it end?"
      },
      {
        "prompt": "Mr. Reyes has 3 liters of juice. He pours it equally into cups that hold 250 milliliters each. How many cups can he fill?"
      },
      {
        "prompt": "Six ribbons have these lengths in inches: 1/4, 1/2, 1/2, 3/4, 1, 1. Make a line plot. Then find the total length of the two 1/2-inch ribbons, and the difference between the longest and shortest ribbons."
      }
    ],
